Depends on task 14. Per P1-1, P1-2 ("Series Layout Shift Fix"), and P1-3: confirmed `next_app/src/components/SeriesSectionClient.tsx:98-101` returns `null` while loading (the comment on line 99 explicitly says this was a deliberate-but-wrong choice: "Optional: loading state or just return null to not jump layout" -- returning `null` is exactly what CAUSES the layout jump the comment claims to avoid) and line 106 (`if (mySeries.length === 0 && joinableSeries.length === 0) return null;`) makes the whole section disappear when empty. There is also currently NO error state at all: the fetch's `catch` block (lines 80-82) silently does `setSeriesList([])` and only `console.error`s -- a failed request is indistinguishable from "no series exist" to the user, with no retry option.

1. Add `const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);` and `import { getLoadErrorMessage } from "@/utils/apiError";` and `import InlineErrorRow from "@/components/InlineErrorRow";` and `import GameCardSkeletonRow from "@/components/GameCardSkeletonRow";`.
2. In the fetch effect (lines 62-91): add `setError(null);` at the start of `run()` (alongside the existing `setLoading(true)` -- note there isn't one today, only `setLoading(true)` at line 66, add it there too), and in the `catch` block (lines 80-82) change `setSeriesList([]);` to also call `setError(getLoadErrorMessage(err));` (keep clearing `seriesList` to `[]` too).
3. Add a `refetch` capability matching the pattern used by every other rail hook in this codebase (`reloadKey` state + `refetch` callback that increments it, included in the fetch effect's dependency array) so `InlineErrorRow`'s retry button has something to call -- see `next_app/src/hooks/useGamesByCity.ts`'s `reloadKey`/`refetch` (lines 15-16 pre-task-3-edits) for the exact shape to copy.
IMPORTANT: this file, unlike the other three rails, doesn't route its loaded output through a single reusable header wrapper -- it renders TWO separate `GamesHorizontalList` blocks ("הקבוצות שלי" / "הצטרפו לקבוצה", lines 122-160) only once data exists. For loading/error/empty states there's no natural single title to reuse (unlike the other three rails' one-rail-one-title shape), so per this component's own shape, wrap loading/error/empty in ONE `GamesHorizontalList` titled `"קבוצות פעילות" (a new umbrella title covering both sub-lists) so a header is still visibly present and stable across all four states (loading, error, empty, loaded) -- do not invent a separate raw `Typography-based heading, reuse `GamesHorizontalList` itself for consistency with tasks 16/17.

4. Replace the loading branch (lines 98-101) with:
```tsx
if (loading) {
  return (
    <GamesHorizontalList title="קבוצות פעילות">
      <GameCardSkeletonRow />
    </GamesHorizontalList>
  );
}
```
5. Add, before the existing `if (mySeries.length === 0 && joinableSeries.length === 0) return null;` check (line 106):
```tsx
if (error) {
  return (
    <GamesHorizontalList title="קבוצות פעילות">
      <Box p={2} width="100%"><InlineErrorRow message={error} onRetry={refetch} /></Box>
    </GamesHorizontalList>
